cff-version: 1.2.0
message: |
  Silverphase is an independent derivative of SpektraLab, the native macOS
  application and C++ Metal render engine built on Andrea Volpato's
  `spektrafilm`. The film simulation, measured profiles and print+scan model
  come from spektrafilm; the original macOS port comes from SpektraLab.

  **If you are citing the science, cite spektrafilm, not this.** The physical
  modelling, the profile measurements and the RA-4 print simulation are that
  project's contribution; see the `references` section below and
  https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm. Cite this repository only when
  you mean the application, the C++ port of the engine, or the GPU pipeline.

  Silverphase code is GPL-3.0-or-later. Andrea Volpato's profiles and their
  derived LUTs are CC BY-SA 4.0. Hanze Qiu's product B&W data and Silverphase
  experimental additions have separate provenance records. Silverphase is
  not affiliated with or endorsed by either original project.

title: "Silverphase: a native Apple application for spectral film and print simulation"
abstract: |
  Silverphase develops a scene-linear photograph through a virtual film
  negative and a print, on the GPU, interactively. It is a SwiftUI application
  for macOS, iPhone and iPad with a shared C++/Metal render engine compiled
  into it. Current validation uses native checks and host workflows; historical
  Python-reference parity results are not current acceptance evidence.
  Silverphase builds on Hanze Qiu's native port; the spectral modelling and
  original measured profiles originate in Andrea Volpato's spektrafilm.

